  "describes_version": "original",
  "as_of": "2013-12-12",
  "sentences": [
   "The bill would allow two people to marry regardless of sex, sexual orientation or gender identity by changing the definition of marriage in federal law.",
   "It would remove the express ban on recognising overseas same-sex marriages and revise the words used by couples and authorised celebrants in marriage ceremonies.",
   "Religious ministers would retain their freedom to decline to solemnise marriages, and the amendments would start on the day after the bill received Royal Assent."
  ],
  "changes": [
   "References to a brother and sister in the prohibited relationships rule would become references to siblings.",
   "The consent table for marriages involving minors would replace husband and wife with gender-neutral wording.",
   "Regulations could make consequential amendments to legislation other than the Marriage Act."
  ],
  "affected": "People seeking marriage, same-sex couples married overseas, authorised celebrants and ministers of religion are affected.",
